# Reference only. The guided first run creates a minimal .env containing the selected provider.
# Copy to an owner-only .env, verify it is untracked and effectively ignored when the project uses
# Git, and leave every unused key absent rather than blank.

# Add only when the connected Traigent run is about to start.
# Portal API keys begin with uk_.
TRAIGENT_API_KEY=

# Use the agent route; another vendor's key does not change its route.
# Name the mismatch; ask to add its key or change provider.
# OpenRouter's gateway and upstream inference provider receive data.
# Fallbacks can change recipients; disclose allowed routes/policy in stage approval.
# For an exact recipient set, disable fallbacks.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Alternatives - chosen provider only.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# COHERE_API_KEY=

# Leave cost settings absent. The assistant uses the installed SDK's per-optimization default and
# one `$5.00` total walkthrough ceiling unless the paid-work approval states otherwise.
# Never persist TRAIGENT_COST_APPROVED here; approval applies only to the current run process.
